1
00:00:00,080 --> 00:00:01,240
Meet DawnPatch.

2
00:00:01,640 --> 00:00:04,780
A local repair workbench that turns a reported browser bug

3
00:00:04,880 --> 00:00:06,380
into evidence you can review.

4
00:00:07,400 --> 00:00:09,840
For this test, we are using Sketch Wild,

5
00:00:09,940 --> 00:00:11,940
an outdoor sketchbook application.

6
00:00:12,460 --> 00:00:14,820
The bug is a deliberately reversed comparison

7
00:00:14,920 --> 00:00:16,580
in an isolated test copy.

8
00:00:17,100 --> 00:00:19,230
Choosing a five minute budget incorrectly

9
00:00:19,240 --> 00:00:20,920
leaves longer missions visible.

10
00:00:21,540 --> 00:00:23,940
The original repository stays unchanged.

11
00:00:24,400 --> 00:00:26,460
We will also check the twenty minute budget

12
00:00:26,500 --> 00:00:29,840
and the location filter, so a partial fix cannot pass.

13
00:00:30,820 --> 00:00:34,240
In Dawn Patch, I start a local repository investigation.

14
00:00:34,700 --> 00:00:36,980
The report describes the behavior we need:

15
00:00:37,420 --> 00:00:39,620
the selected time is a maximum budget,

16
00:00:39,780 --> 00:00:42,040
and shorter missions must remain available.

17
00:00:42,660 --> 00:00:45,100
This gives the repair agent a clear requirement,

18
00:00:45,300 --> 00:00:47,700
rather than just saying that a screen is broken.

19
00:00:48,600 --> 00:00:51,980
Next, I record the browser steps and the expected results.

20
00:00:52,580 --> 00:00:54,540
These checks cover the five minute limit,

21
00:00:54,840 --> 00:00:56,800
all six missions within twenty minutes,

22
00:00:57,060 --> 00:00:59,260
and the four missions available in a courtyard.

23
00:00:59,800 --> 00:01:02,580
The exact same steps will run against both copies.

24
00:01:03,180 --> 00:01:05,060
The selected engine is local Gemma,

25
00:01:05,160 --> 00:01:08,090
coordinated through Mastra, with source edits kept

26
00:01:08,100 --> 00:01:09,680
in an isolated workspace.

27
00:01:10,540 --> 00:01:13,320
Local Gemma attempted the repair through Mastra.

28
00:01:13,740 --> 00:01:16,220
Its proposals repeated the existing code,

29
00:01:16,340 --> 00:01:17,980
so Dawn Patch rejected them.

30
00:01:18,260 --> 00:01:20,820
The model did not solve this case autonomously.

31
00:01:21,440 --> 00:01:23,460
I supplied a reviewed correction next,

32
00:01:23,640 --> 00:01:26,060
and the workbench verified it independently.

33
00:01:26,580 --> 00:01:29,600
The long local processing wait is removed from this edit.

34
00:01:30,600 --> 00:01:32,820
Here is the developer assisted correction.

35
00:01:33,240 --> 00:01:34,920
The time budget is a maximum,

36
00:01:35,060 --> 00:01:37,330
so the duration comparison must include

37
00:01:37,340 --> 00:01:38,900
missions at or below it.

38
00:01:39,360 --> 00:01:42,690
Dawn Patch labels the correction clearly and applies it only

39
00:01:42,700 --> 00:01:44,120
to an isolated copy.

40
00:01:45,080 --> 00:01:48,000
The corrected candidate has now passed verification.

41
00:01:48,480 --> 00:01:50,480
This is a developer assisted result,

42
00:01:50,620 --> 00:01:52,520
with independent browser evidence.

43
00:01:53,160 --> 00:01:56,300
The original repository has not been changed or published.

44
00:01:57,200 --> 00:01:59,410
On the corrected website, five minutes now

45
00:01:59,420 --> 00:02:00,940
shows exactly one mission.

46
00:02:01,500 --> 00:02:02,930
Twenty minutes restores all

47
00:02:02,940 --> 00:02:04,940
six, including shorter tasks.

48
00:02:05,600 --> 00:02:08,319
Choosing the courtyard keeps four eligible missions.

49
00:02:08,800 --> 00:02:12,120
These checks confirm that the fix preserves the location filter

50
00:02:12,220 --> 00:02:13,680
as well as the time boundary.

51
00:02:14,660 --> 00:02:18,110
Back in Dawn Patch, the evidence view preserves the baseline

52
00:02:18,120 --> 00:02:20,820
and candidate captures from real Chromium runs.

53
00:02:21,320 --> 00:02:24,100
The comparison slider helps review what changed.

54
00:02:24,560 --> 00:02:27,760
The pass or fail result comes from the recorded assertions,

55
00:02:28,040 --> 00:02:30,080
rather than from how a screenshot looks.

56
00:02:31,080 --> 00:02:33,210
The patch is small: one comparison

57
00:02:33,220 --> 00:02:34,740
changes in the mission filter.

58
00:02:35,200 --> 00:02:37,830
Dependencies, credentials, mission content,

59
00:02:37,840 --> 00:02:40,040
and configuration remain untouched.

60
00:02:40,520 --> 00:02:43,120
The source diff is available for review and export.

61
00:02:44,100 --> 00:02:46,280
The checks confirm a failing baseline,

62
00:02:46,440 --> 00:02:50,160
a successful isolated build, and a passing candidate replay.

63
00:02:50,720 --> 00:02:52,730
The same eight recorded steps ran

64
00:02:52,740 --> 00:02:54,380
before and after the change.

65
00:02:54,940 --> 00:02:58,260
Broader application behavior still needs its own tests.

66
00:02:59,300 --> 00:03:01,340
That is Dawn Patch: reproduce,

67
00:03:01,440 --> 00:03:03,500
repair, verify, and review.

68
00:03:04,100 --> 00:03:06,980
This demonstration shows a real Sketch Wild test

69
00:03:07,060 --> 00:03:09,600
with a clearly labeled developer assisted correction,

70
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:12,210
rather than claiming an autonomous fix that

71
00:03:12,220 --> 00:03:13,640
the model did not produce.
